  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.15171v2</id>
    <title>A Response to paper Critical Evaluation of Studies Alleging Evidence for Technosignatures in the POSS1-E Photographic Plates by Watters et al. (2026)</title>
    <updated>2026-04-30T14:26:56Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.15171v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.15171v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We respond to the critique by Watters et al. (2026) of the statistical analyses in Villarroel et al. (2025) and Bruehl &amp; Villarroel (2025). We argue that the critique conflates object-level validation with ensemble-level statistical inference and relies on a reduced, heterogeneously filtered subset originally constructed for a different scientific purpose. We further question whether the aggressively filtered subset used in Watters et al. (2026) demonstrates a meaningful improvement in sample purity, given the twenty-fold reduction in sample size. Our simple, visual check does not suggest that it does. The subset further lacks complete temporal information and is seriously statistically underpowered for testing the reported Earth-shadow deficit. We emphasise that the horizontal separation metric used for plate assignment and time reconstruction as in Watters et al. (2026) depends on the inclusion of the cos(Dec) factor to ensure geometric consistency. Any omission would alter plate assignment and inferred observation times. Moreover, the analyses presented in Watters et al. (2026) do not include uncertainty estimates or error propagation, limiting the interpretability of the claimed null results. We conclude that the principal findings reported in Villarroel et al. (2025) and Bruehl &amp; Villarroel (2025) are not invalidated by the analyses presented in Watters et al. (2026).</summary>
    <category term="astro-ph.IM" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="astro-ph.SR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-02-16T20:21:37Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>A response to Watters et al. 2026, arXiv:2601.21946</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="astro-ph.IM"/>
    <author>
      <name>Beatriz Villarroel</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Alina Streblyanska</name>
    </author>
